WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:06.500
Title card appears: "Introduction to databases and modern digital learning". A speaker stands at the lecture podium.

00:18.000 --> 00:23.000
The speaker gestures toward a screen displaying icons for Google, YouTube, and Wikipedia.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.500
A chart displays online learning statistics showing the average video length is 4 minutes and 12 seconds.

00:50.000 --> 00:55.500
On screen: A lecture slide referencing Professor Michael Wesch's study on digital culture and YouTube.

01:12.000 --> 01:17.500
A split screen compares a monolithic 60-minute lecture with modular, digestible 4-minute concept chapters.

01:32.000 --> 01:37.000
Diagram illustrates how bite-sized learning chunks improve knowledge retention and focus for diverse learners.

01:50.000 --> 01:56.000
Summary slide reinforces that modern accessible education thrives in focused, high-clarity learning segments.
